      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Gus and Marnie Lund kept the Northwoods open after the Cordon shut Route 9, because the convoy drivers paid in diesel and news. Convoy 6 stopped at the Mile 9 roadblock and its crews were quartered over the bar; one of them was already shaking. When the drivers started to turn, the Lunds made the bar room the quarantine: they nailed the front doors shut from outside, locked the kitchen door, boarded the cellar stair from the hall, and came and went by the beer hatch on the north side. Three nights ago Gus went down the hatch for water and came back up through the trapdoor behind the bar instead, his keys still on him. Marnie locked herself in the apartment upstairs, rigged her shotgun to the door, wrote to their daughter and stopped answering.",
